The crash occurs in `subsys/bluetooth/audio/cap_initiator.c` within the `bt_cap_initiator_enabled` function, specifically at line 1916: `__ASSERT(proc_param != NULL, "proc is not done, but could not get next proc_param");`.

This assertion indicates a logical inconsistency: the procedure is not yet marked as complete (`!bt_cap_common_proc_is_done()` is true), but the `get_next_proc_param()` function returns `NULL`, implying there are no more streams on which to initiate the current sub-procedure (BT_CAP_COMMON_SUBPROC_TYPE_ENABLE).

